# The data partition (OS-KEYS.md). Opens by itself with this machine's TPM; on any other machine it asks
# for the recovery key, for as long as it takes (tries=0, no device timeout: disk-setup may be waiting
# for a person). A TPM the firmware reports but Linux has not found yet gets 2 minutes (token-timeout,
# matching disk-setup's TOKEN_WAIT_S): a slow chip or driver; a missing one is asked
# at once. try-empty-password opens a disk whose setup recorded the choice to go unencrypted.
medbrains-data PARTLABEL=medbrains-data none luks,tpm2-device=auto,try-empty-password=yes,tries=0,token-timeout=120s,x-systemd.device-timeout=0
